39.1,1987,70,83,21],[29474,29.7,2013,64,96,24],[29475,32.7,2013,67,88,20],[29476,34.1,1987,68,90,17],[29775,41.9,1987,71,94,17]],"links":[["Fremont County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/idaho/fremont-county"],["ARC or PLC in Fremont County","/arc-plc/idaho/fremont-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and July to August came in under 90% of normal in 38 of them on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 18 grids, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 38% of normal for June to July and 58% for May to June. The 2026 numbers so far are low too, with February to March at 54% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 28573 had its driest year in 2001 at 57% of normal.</p>"}
